# Active development stack (Nevernote)

## Default (prioritize this)

- **UI and product logic**: [`NeverNote/`](NeverNote/) — SwiftUI app entry in `NevernoteApp.swift`, screens in `ContentView.swift`, models in `Item.swift` (paths as referenced by [`Nevernote.xcodeproj`](Nevernote.xcodeproj)).
- **Build / run**: Project [`Nevernote.xcodeproj`](Nevernote.xcodeproj), scheme **NeverNote**, iOS Simulator (see [`.cursor/skills/build/SKILL.md`](.cursor/skills/build/SKILL.md)).

## Legacy (do not extend by default)

- **[`NeverNote1/`](NeverNote1/)** — UIKit / Objective-C sources, plist, storyboards, and assets used by the existing target. Treat as **frozen / reference-only** for migration and build compatibility.
- **Do not** implement new features, refactors, or styling changes under `NeverNote1/` unless the user **explicitly** asks, or the change is required to fix a **build break** or **blocking runtime bug** in shipped code.
- When the user asks for app behavior or visuals, implement in **SwiftUI under `NeverNote/`** first.

## Tests

- [`NeverNoteTests/`](NeverNoteTests/) is legacy Objective-C XCTest. Prefer adding new coverage alongside SwiftUI work only when the user requests tests; do not expand Obj-C tests by default.
